### Describe the bug

While migrating a project to Vite 8, I noticed that some plugins are applied in dev mode but not when building the application. It seems like more glob features are supported in dev but not when building.

### Reproduction

https://stackblitz.com/edit/vitejs-vite-cpcsqnn4?file=vite.config.ts

### Steps to reproduce

Create a new Vite project with the vanilla template and add the following `vite.config.ts` file:
```ts
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';

export default defineConfig({
    plugins: [
        {
            name: 'filter-test',
            transform: {
                filter: {
                    id: {
                        include: '**/*.(js)',
                    }
                },
                handler(code, id) {
                    console.log('transform', id);
                }
            }
        }
    ],
});
```
During dev the filter is applied to all javascript files, but it is not applied to any file during build.

Note that `**/*.js` would be applied at dev and build, so my guess is that the `()` syntax is not supported in rolldown. But I would expect the hook filter to behave the same in dev.

